yes(494,'A','T has atomic number 16, so it represents sulfur, a solid nonmetal at room temperature. R (13) is aluminium, J (8) is oxygen and X (4) is beryllium. The two metals and gaseous oxygen do not satisfy the description.',['https://periodic-table.rsc.org/element/16/sulfur'],question='A section of the periodic table labels elements by letter. Their atomic numbers are L = 2, G = 3, X = 4, J = 8, E = 9, M = 12, R = 13 and T = 16. Which letter represents a nonmetal that is solid at room temperature?',options=['T','R','J','X'],audit='Transcribed all letter/atomic-number mappings from visually inspected PDF44 table. X occupies atomic-number4 cell. Corrected old B to A; no absent-diagram dependency.',check='periodic-mapping')
