yes(511,'A','A negative ΔH means the forward reaction releases heat. Lowering temperature favours this exothermic direction, increasing the equilibrium proportion of products. This describes the equilibrium shift, not the speed of reaction.',['https://openstax.org/books/chemistry-2e/pages/13-3-shifting-equilibria-le-chateliers-principle'],question='For a reaction at equilibrium with ΔH < 0, which temperature condition favours the forward equilibrium direction?',options=['Low temperature','High temperature','All temperatures','All pressures'],audit='Clarified equilibrium favourability instead of universal spontaneity; corrected old B to A.',check='exothermic-shift')
